index 0000000..5f96a74
--- /dev/null
+++ b/docs/SHARED-SIG.md
@@ -0,0 +1,13 @@
+# Shared native SIG adapter and intermediate CLI report
+
+shared_sig::Graph owns one vertex ID allocator, source-key map and relation ID store across GRID, beam candidates, beam groups, rests and serifs. Source identity is (system, phase, local ID). Imports retain original payload and source identity while rewriting vertex and relation endpoints to shared IDs. IDs allocate in actual import/registration encounter order, are not reused, and remain stable across re-synchronization and cleanup. GRID and BEAMS glyph IDs retain explicit separate namespaces; no shared glyph-index equivalence is claimed.
+
+GRID import reads actual native bar_semantics systems/inters/relations. Beam sync uses typed SystemCandidates in registration order, including tombstones. Full system sync adds group vertices/Containment/support relations and rest/serif vertices/relations. Converted rests keep an explicit source_beam_id pointing to the source beam's shared tombstone. Rest relation source/target kinds and side are checked; dangling or removed endpoints, duplicate GRID source IDs, duplicate rest/group IDs and budget overflow reject. Clone/commit updates make imports and sync transactional. Existing phase logic remains authoritative; this store is the common graph adapter/view, not a replacement JVM SIG engine. Initial-candidate-only sync rejects after live group/rest data exists, requiring a complete snapshot to prevent stale memberships.
+
+multiple_rest_pipeline::process_shared synchronizes initial candidate/group identities, calls the existing native conversion pass, then synchronizes its registration and cleanup. All eleven unchanged original conversion controls (six positive, five negative) still match; the tests also check unified relation endpoints and rest vertex/relation counts. Four additional contract tests cover collisions across GRID/beam/group/rest IDs, deterministic replay, stable tombstones, malformed endpoint/duplicate rollback, cross-system local ID reuse and protection against incomplete later-phase updates. Eleven focused tests, fmt and all-targets Clippy pass.
+
+The existing beam-spots CLI now retains typed native candidate state and emits shared_sig beside existing phase reports. Actual raster input beams-single.png completes the native path and produces one GRID vertex and one beam vertex with distinct common IDs. A second fresh CLI run at the final code matches the complete prior report byte content/hash and shared IDs. This CLI report covers GRID and BEAMS.INITIAL_CANDIDATES only; it does not run later extensions/hooks/groups/rest conversion. musicxml_complete remains false. Input/report hashes, actual commands, both logs and shared graph output are preserved in evidence.
+
+Current full debug/release suites are UNVERIFIED at this new tree. The 289-test full release result belongs solely to parent source 21f0833abd67dd4fa1dd0c60a74a686779329818, immutable remote checkpoint a14eb873873b101247913c41a6987cdbddaa17d4. No broad regression rerun was requested for this adapter stage.
+
+Remaining: CLI execution of the complete BEAMS/rest pipeline with native staff/pitch and system lag mapping, common contextualization beyond existing GRID classes, integrating header/stem/other inter namespaces, full shared glyph index, journal/snapshot rehydration (replay currently rebuilds from ordered phase inputs), additional error-path and large/multi-staff controls, real-score rest recognition and full OMR. Shared IDs deliberately differ from JVM IDs; deterministic replay requires the same phase/source registration order.
